Name: DecayRiv
Year: 2026
Summary: Lambda -> p pi- candidates: full combinatorics, the mass window, and the one-to-one matching
Experiment: MC
Collider: any    # no Beams line: any beams (the Lambda card collides Ne-20 on Ne-20)
Status: UNVALIDATED NOHEPDATA SINGLEWEIGHT
Reentrant: true
Authors:
 - Rajnoor S. Brar
References:
 - 'Ported from an earlier standalone module'
RunInfo: 'Any hadronic collision in which Lambda is allowed to decay to p pi-. The generator card
  must enable that decay (3122:onIfMatch = 2212 -211) or there is nothing to reconstruct.'
Options:
 - SET=all,unvalidated,validated,selected  # which candidate set to record; 'all' books all three,
                                           # prefixed. A named set books the same seven
                                           # distributions unprefixed, so the three can be swept
                                           # across and drawn as curves on one page.
 - MASSTOL=#      # |m(p pi) - m(Lambda)| accepted in GeV (default 0.15)
 - COSTHETATOL=#  # 0 = off; else |cos(theta*) + 1| tolerance (default 0.0)
 - RESERVED=#     # beam protons per event that cannot come from a Lambda, 2 x Z (default 2, pp)
 - TRACKPTMIN=#   # track pT threshold in GeV (default 0.0)
 - TRACKETAMAX=#  # track |eta| acceptance (default 8.0)
 - BINS=#         # bins per distribution (default 100)
 - MASSAXIS=#     # half-width of the mass axis about m(Lambda) in GeV (default 0.4)
 - ENERGYAXIS=#   # upper edge of the energy axis in GeV (default 200)
 - MOMENTUMAXIS=# # upper edge of the momentum axis in GeV (default 200)
 - PTAXIS=#       # upper edge of the pT axis in GeV (default 20)
 - ETAAXIS=#      # half-width of the eta axis (default 8)
 - COUNTAXIS=#    # highest candidate multiplicity binned (default 50)
Description:
  'Reconstructs Lambda -> p pi- from final-state protons and negative pions, and records three
   nested candidate sets: every (p, pi-) pair (unvalidated), the pairs inside the mass window
   (validated), and the greedy one-to-one matching that takes the best mass agreement first and
   never reuses a track (selected). Each set carries the invariant mass, energy, momentum,
   transverse and longitudinal momentum, pseudorapidity, and the per-event candidate count.

   The reconstruction itself is shared verbatim with the C++ module of the same measurement
   (modules/Decay/Reconstruction.hh), so running both on one sample compares the two analysis
   paths rather than two implementations of the physics.'
ValidationInfo:
  'Compared against modules/Decay/Decay.cc on identical events; the two fill the same
   distributions from the same shared reconstruction.'
Keywords: [strangeness, lambda, invariant mass]
